# Xcode
build/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
*.moved-aside
# ...but xcshareddata is the *other* half of that directory pair, and it must
# stay tracked. Xcode autocreates a per-user scheme under xcuserdata/ the
# first time you open a project, which works fine locally and then vanishes
# on a fresh clone — that is why `xcodebuild -scheme testExample` used to fail
# for everyone but the original author. The shared scheme lives in
# testExample.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/xcschemes/ and is committed deliberately.
!*.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/
*.pbxuser
!default.pbxuser
*.mode1v3
!default.mode1v3
*.mode2v3
*.perspectivev3

# Swift Package Manager
.build/
.swiftpm/

# macOS
.DS_Store
